  "question": {
    "text": "The radius of the second Bohr orbit, in terms of the Bohr radius <math> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>(a</mtext></mrow> <mtext>0</mtext> </msub> <mtext>)</mtext></mrow> </math>, of <math><mtext>L</mtext><msup><mrow><mtext>i</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is given as <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> . Find the sum of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math> here?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.529</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><math> <mrow>  <mtext>r</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac>   <mrow>    <msub>     <mtext>a</mtext>     <mtext>0</mtext>    </msub>    <mo>&#x00D7;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow>   <mn>3</mn>  </mfrac>  <mo>=</mo><mfrac>   <mrow>    <mn>4</mn><msub>     <mtext>a</mtext>     <mtext>0</mtext>    </msub>    </mrow>   <mn>3</mn>  </mfrac>  </mrow></math><br />Hence <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br />So, sum of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>"
  }
